  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "Supplying the periodic-graph background still leaves a genuine source-local mechanism: the ambient space is partitioned into the facet-cone pieces attached to the faces of a triangulation of the growth polytope, and the explicit well-arranged conditions supply half-open lattice parallelepipeds on which shortest-path distances are exactly additive. The counted proof converts that additivity into the opposite-cone rational identities, and these yield both the denominator LCM description with the controlled numerator degree of the growth series and the reciprocity G_s(1/t)=(-1)^n G_s(t), with assertion (1) derived from the denominator (1-t)Q_2. This direct well-arranged-graph reciprocity argument is structurally different from the shifted-dilation Ehrhart quasipolynomial criterion and is above ordinary PhD qualifying material.",
